From 636e66e2c032ad32a7f21ec7ea5389b00ae42b90
Subject: Add per-invocation response channel + multi-take queue to ConsoleCommand
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy-console/commit/636e66e2c032ad32a7f21ec7ea5389b00ae42b90
Date: 2026-06-04T13:23:07+01:00

ConsoleCommandEntered gains an optional ConsoleResponder (a result sink).
ConsoleCommand's reply methods resolve the responder when present (buffering
reply lines), or write PrintConsoleLine as before. take() drains a queue of all
matching invocations this frame: single-execution handlers take one and the
rest are re-emitted via SystemParam::apply to be retried next frame, while a
handler can `while let Some(Ok(c)) = cmd.take()` to process every concurrent
invocation in one frame. Parse errors are reported (to the responder or console)
and skipped.
